Current design (details):

Pscf::ParameterModifer 

   Base class for classes that can modify a specialized parameter.
   Provides an interface for getting and setting parameter values.
   Lists of associated integer ids are represented as arrays.

Pscf::ParameterType

   Type of parameter that can be varied or swept.
   Has name identifier string, and nId (# of required int ids).
   Has a pointer to an associated ParameterModifier.

Pscf::SweepTmpl:

   public:

      // Interface for list of ParameterType objects
      addParameterType (overloaded)
      addParameterTypes
 
   protected:
 
      // Interface for Lagrange state extrapolation
      state(int i)
      s(int i)
      c(int i)
      historySize()
      historyCapacity();
      setCoefficients();
      (also extrapolate and accept)
 
      // Interface for sweep
      void solve() => defines a skeleton algorithm
 
      setParameters(double sNew) = 0;
      extrapolate(double sNew) = 0;
      void getSolution() = 0; (called by accept)
      void reset() = 0;

   private:

      accept():
       -> Updates extrapolator state and history
       -> Calls getSolution
  
Pscf::Rp::Sweep

   void setup()
      calls SweepTmpl::initialize();
      Proposal: Make pure virtual in base class. Implement in SweepTmpl.

   void extrapolate():
      Implements this function
      Creates a linear superposition of states.
      Proposal: Move to SweepTmpl subclass, or below.

   void setParameters() override (empty function - for testing only)
      Comment: Actually implemented in LinearSweep subclass
      Proposal: Keep implementation in a lower-level subclass

   void getSolution() override;
      Calls State::setSystem
      Calls State::getSystemState
      Calls outputSolution
      Calls outputSummary(logFile_)
      Note: Implementation depends on state representation
      Proposal:
